  <script type="application/ld+json" slot="head">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How much does boiler installation cost in Liverpool?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "A like-for-like combi boiler installation in Liverpool starts from £1,800 fully fitted. System boilers start from £2,200 and regular boilers from £2,500. All prices include the energy efficient A-rated boiler, installation, smart controls, Benchmark certificate and Gas Safe certificate. The Checkatrade average for Liverpool is £1,677 to £2,733. Call 0151 558 0334 for a free fixed-price survey." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Can I install my own boiler?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No. It is illegal to install a gas boiler yourself unless you are Gas Safe registered. All gas boiler installation must be carried out by a Gas Safe registered engineer. An incorrectly installed boiler is a serious carbon monoxide risk. Always verify your engineer at gassaferegister.co.uk before any gas work." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "What size boiler do I need for my Liverpool home?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "A 1 to 2 bed Liverpool flat or terraced house typically needs a 24 to 28kW combi boiler. A 3-bed semi needs 28 to 32kW. Larger properties with multiple bathrooms need 32 to 40kW or a system boiler. We size the boiler at the free survey based on your property, radiators and hot water demand." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "What is the difference between combi, system and regular boilers?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "A combi boiler heats water on demand and needs no tank or cylinder. Best for most 1 to 3 bed Liverpool homes. A system boiler stores hot water in a cylinder but needs no cold water tank. Best for larger homes with more than one bathroom. A regular boiler (also called conventional or heat-only) needs both a hot water cylinder and a cold water tank in the loft. Common in older Liverpool properties with gravity-fed systems." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Are there complications with older Liverpool properties?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Liverpool has one of the highest concentrations of Victorian and Edwardian housing in England. Many have gravity-fed systems, back boilers, chimneys used as flue routes and pipe runs that differ from modern builds. Our engineers know Liverpool's housing stock well and spot complications before opening a wall. The free survey is essential for any older Liverpool property." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How long does boiler installation take in Liverpool?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "A like-for-like combi swap takes 4 to 6 hours and is done in one day. Bigger jobs take 1 to 3 days. Same-day and next-day install is available for urgent swaps. We confirm timing at the free survey." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "What warranty do I get with a new boiler?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Every install carries a 12-month workmanship guarantee for peace of mind. The manufacturer warranty depends on the boiler model and installer accreditation. Standard manufacturer warranties typically run 2 to 5 years on most models. Longer warranties up to 10 years are offered by Worcester Bosch and Vaillant when fitted by an accredited installer and serviced yearly. We register the manufacturer warranty on your behalf on install day." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Do I need a power flush before a new boiler?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "In most cases yes. All major makers need a clean system as a warranty condition. We do the power flush before connecting the new boiler. A power flush costs from £350 and comes as a bundle with your new boiler at a better combined price." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Is there a grant for a new boiler in Liverpool?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Liverpool homeowners on qualifying benefits may be eligible for the ECO4 scheme for a free boiler replacement. The Boiler Upgrade Scheme provides up to £7,500 towards a heat pump. We check eligibility at the free survey at no cost to you." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Are you Gas Safe registered?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Liverpool Emergency Plumber is Gas Safe registered. Verify at gassaferegister.co.uk. Every install is done by Gas Safe registered engineers. All gas work is carried out by Gas Safe registered engineers." } }
    ]
  }
  </script>

