  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Signs Your Liverpool Boiler Needs Replacing</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">If your boiler is over 10 years old or showing any of these signs, a new energy efficient boiler is worth thinking about.</p>
      <div class="pf-signs" style="margin-top:2rem;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:1rem;">
        <div class="pf-sign" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #dc2626;border-radius:10px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;"><strong style="display:block;color:#1a3a5c;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Boiler is over 10 to 12 years old</strong><p style="margin:0;">Modern A-rated energy efficient boilers run at 90 to 94% efficiency. A boiler from before 2010 runs at 65 to 70%. A new boiler almost always pays back faster than more repairs.</p></div>
        <div class="pf-sign" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #dc2626;border-radius:10px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;"><strong style="display:block;color:#1a3a5c;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Repair bills are stacking up</strong><p style="margin:0;">Spending more than £200 to £300 a year on repairs? A new boiler will likely pay for itself in a few years. £1,800 fitted beats years of growing repair costs.</p></div>
        <div class="pf-sign" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #dc2626;border-radius:10px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;"><strong style="display:block;color:#1a3a5c;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Boiler breaks down when you need it most</strong><p style="margin:0;">If your boiler fails in a cold snap, the heat exchanger or internal parts are likely failing. Old boilers struggle most when demand is high. Replace before it goes cold for peace of mind.</p></div>
        <div class="pf-sign" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #dc2626;border-radius:10px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;"><strong style="display:block;color:#1a3a5c;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Energy bills rising for no reason</strong><p style="margin:0;">A boiler losing efficiency burns more gas for the same heat. If bills rise but your usage has not changed, your boiler is working harder than it should.</p></div>
        <div class="pf-sign" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #dc2626;border-radius:10px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;"><strong style="display:block;color:#1a3a5c;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Odd noises from the boiler</strong><p style="margin:0;">Banging, kettling, whistling or gurgling sounds point to internal problems. In an older boiler these often mean replacement is cheaper than repair.</p></div>
        <div class="pf-sign" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #dc2626;border-radius:10px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;"><strong style="display:block;color:#1a3a5c;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Pilot light keeps going out</strong><p style="margin:0;">On older boilers a pilot light that keeps going out usually means a faulty thermocouple or carbon build-up. In a boiler over 10 years old this is a strong sign to replace.</p></div>
        <div class="pf-sign" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #dc2626;border-radius:10px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;"><strong style="display:block;color:#1a3a5c;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Yellow or orange flame instead of blue</strong><p style="margin:0;">A healthy gas flame is blue. Yellow or orange means incomplete combustion and a possible CO risk. Stop using the boiler now and call a <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gas Safe registered</a> engineer. If you think it is a gas emergency, call <a href="https://cadentgas.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cadent Gas on 0800 111 999</a> first.</p></div>
        <div class="pf-sign" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #dc2626;border-radius:10px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;"><strong style="display:block;color:#1a3a5c;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">EPC rating of F or G</strong><p style="margin:0;">An old boiler is the top cause of a poor EPC rating. A new A-rated energy efficient boiler is the single biggest step to a better EPC. A better EPC can add 14% to property value. See the <a href="https://www.gov.uk/find-energy-certificate" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GOV.UK EPC checker</a>.</p></div>
        <div class="pf-sign" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #dc2626;border-radius:10px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;"><strong style="display:block;color:#1a3a5c;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">No Gas Safe certificate on record</strong><p style="margin:0;">No certificate on record means no proof it was fitted legally. A new install gives you full paperwork. A Benchmark certificate and Gas Safe certificate on the same day.</p></div>
      </div>

      <div style="background:#f97316;border-radius:10px;padding:1.5rem;text-align:center;margin-top:2rem;">
        <p style="color:#ffffff;font-weight:700;font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Spot two or more signs? Your boiler very likely needs replacing. Book a free survey today.</p>
