        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #f97316;border-radius:10px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;display:flex;gap:0.75rem;"><span class="pf-who-icon" style="color:#f97316;font-weight:900;flex-shrink:0;font-size:1.1rem;">●</span><div><strong>Combi boilers</strong><p>A combi boiler heats hot water on demand from the mains. No tank or cylinder needed. The most common choice in 1 to 3 bed Liverpool homes. From £1,800 fitted. Compact, simple and the cheapest type to install.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #f97316;border-radius:10px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;display:flex;gap:0.75rem;"><span class="pf-who-icon" style="color:#f97316;font-weight:900;flex-shrink:0;font-size:1.1rem;">●</span><div><strong>System boilers</strong><p>A system boiler heats hot water and stores it in a cylinder. No cold tank needed in the loft. The best pick for larger Liverpool homes with two or more bathrooms. Steady hot water at multiple taps at once. From £2,200 fitted.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #f97316;border-radius:10px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;display:flex;gap:0.75rem;"><span class="pf-who-icon" style="color:#f97316;font-weight:900;flex-shrink:0;font-size:1.1rem;">●</span><div><strong>Regular boilers</strong><p>A regular boiler, also called a conventional boiler or heat-only boiler, needs a hot water cylinder and a cold water tank in the loft. The right fit for older Liverpool properties with gravity-fed systems. Common in Victorian and Edwardian homes in Aigburth, Allerton, Sefton Park and Crosby. Regular boilers from £2,500 fitted.</p></div></div>
      </div>

      <div style="background:#fff7ed;border:1px solid #fed7aa;border-left:4px solid #f97316;border-radius:10px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin-top:2rem;text-align:center;">
        <p style="color:#1a3a5c;font-size:0.88rem;margin:0;font-weight:600;">Not sure which boiler type fits? The free survey confirms the best option for your Liverpool property based on the rooms, bathrooms and existing system.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

