        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes" style="background:#f1f5f9;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #16a34a;border-radius:10px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;display:flex;gap:0.75rem;"><span class="pf-who-icon" style="color:#16a34a;font-weight:900;flex-shrink:0;font-size:1.1rem;">✓</span><div><strong>3 bed semi or terrace. 28 to 32kW</strong><p>The most common Liverpool home type. Found across Aigburth, Wavertree, West Derby, Allerton and Childwall. A 28kW or 32kW combi covers most of these.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes" style="background:#f1f5f9;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #16a34a;border-radius:10px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;display:flex;gap:0.75rem;"><span class="pf-who-icon" style="color:#16a34a;font-weight:900;flex-shrink:0;font-size:1.1rem;">✓</span><div><strong>4 or 5 bed property or multiple bathrooms. 32 to 40kW or system boiler</strong><p>Larger Liverpool homes in Woolton, Formby, Heswall and Crosby. Or homes with two or more bathrooms. May need a 36 to 40kW combi or a system boiler with hot water cylinder for steady hot water.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes" style="background:#f1f5f9;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #16a34a;border-radius:10px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;display:flex;gap:0.75rem;"><span class="pf-who-icon" style="color:#16a34a;font-weight:900;flex-shrink:0;font-size:1.1rem;">✓</span><div><strong>Victorian or Edwardian property with gravity-fed system. Regular boiler</strong><p>Many of Liverpool's older homes in Sefton Park, Mossley Hill, Aigburth and Crosby have gravity-fed systems not suited to combi boilers. A regular boiler with hot water cylinder and cold tank in the loft is often the right pick. Our engineers are experienced with these older systems.</p></div></div>
