      <h2>Boiler Installation in Liverpool's Older Properties</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Liverpool has one of the highest concentrations of Victorian and Edwardian housing in England. We know every type.</p>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-navy" style="margin-top:2rem;background:#1a3a5c;border-radius:10px;padding:1.5rem;color:#ffffff;">
        <h3 style="color:#ffffff;">What Makes Liverpool Properties Different</h3>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.9);">Many of Liverpool's Victorian terraces, Georgian townhouses and Edwardian semis were built with gravity-fed heating systems. Back boilers behind fires. Chimneys used as flue routes. Pipe runs that differ from modern builds. Areas like Aigburth, Allerton, Sefton Park, Mossley Hill, Crosby and Woolton have many of these older property types.</p>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.9);">A boiler installer without Liverpool experience can get the cost wrong or fit the wrong system. We have worked across Liverpool's housing stock for years and know what to anticipate before we open a wall. The free survey is essential for any older Liverpool property because we spot problems before they become surprises on install day.</p>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.9);">For more on gas install safety rules in older homes, see <a href="https://www.hse.gov.uk/gas/domestic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">HSE domestic gas safety guidance</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-orange" style="margin-top:2rem;background:#fff7ed;border:1px solid #fed7aa;border-left:4px solid #f97316;border-radius:10px;padding:1.5rem;">
        <h3>Can I Install My Own Boiler?</h3>
        <p>No. It is illegal to install a gas boiler yourself unless you are Gas Safe registered. All gas boiler work, including install, replacement and some repairs, must be done by a <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gas Safe registered engineer</a>. A wrongly fitted boiler is a serious carbon monoxide, gas leak and fire risk. Always check your engineer's Gas Safe number before any gas work. See <a href="https://www.hse.gov.uk/gas/domestic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">HSE guidance on domestic gas safety</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

