      <div class="pf-card pf-card-orange" style="margin-top:2rem;background:#fff7ed;border:1px solid #fed7aa;border-left:4px solid #f97316;border-radius:10px;padding:1.5rem;">
        <h3 style="text-align:center;">Why a Power Flush Before Your New Boiler Matters</h3>
        <p>All major boiler makers including Worcester Bosch and <a href="https://www.vaillant.co.uk/for-installers/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vaillant</a> need a clean system as a warranty condition. Sludge and magnetite from your old system can damage the new heat exchanger in months if not removed first. Under Boiler Plus regulations, installers must also confirm the system is clean and efficient at install.</p>
        <p>We do the power flush before the new boiler is fitted, not after. This protects the heat exchanger from day one and keeps your warranty intact for full peace of mind. A power flush costs from £350 and comes as a bundle with your new boiler at a better combined price. Ask when you call to book your survey.</p>
