      <p class="pf-sub">Straight answers to what Liverpool homeowners and landlords ask most before they book.</p>
      <div class="pf-faq" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.5rem;">
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does boiler installation cost in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>A like-for-like combi boiler installation in Liverpool starts from £1,800 fully fitted. System boilers start from £2,200. Regular boilers from £2,500. All prices include the energy efficient A-rated boiler, install, smart controls, magnetic filter, system flush, Benchmark certificate and Gas Safe certificate. The <a href="https://www.checkatrade.com/blog/cost-guides/new-boiler-cost/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Checkatrade average for Liverpool</a> is £1,677 to £2,733. We give a written fixed-price quote after the free survey.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">LEGAL</span>&nbsp; Can I install my own boiler?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>No. It is illegal to install a gas boiler yourself unless you are Gas Safe registered. All gas boiler install must be done by a <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gas Safe registered engineer</a>. A wrongly fitted boiler is a serious carbon monoxide and gas leak risk. Always check your engineer's Gas Safe number before any gas work. See <a href="https://www.hse.gov.uk/gas/domestic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">HSE domestic gas safety guidance</a>.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">TYPES</span>&nbsp; What is the difference between combi, system and regular boilers?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>A combi boiler heats hot water on demand. No tank or cylinder needed. Best for most 1 to 3 bed Liverpool homes. A system boiler stores hot water in a cylinder. No cold tank needed. Best for larger homes with more than one bathroom. A regular boiler, also called a conventional boiler or heat-only boiler, needs both a hot water cylinder and a cold water tank in the loft. Common in older Liverpool properties with gravity-fed systems.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">SIZE</span>&nbsp; What size boiler do I need for my Liverpool home?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>Boiler output is measured in kilowatts. A 1 to 2 bed Liverpool home usually needs a 24 to 28kW combi. A 3-bed semi needs 28 to 32kW. Larger homes with multiple bathrooms need 32 to 40kW or a system boiler. Older Liverpool properties with gravity-fed systems often need regular boilers. We size it at the free survey based on your property, radiators and hot water demand. Wrong size is one of the top install mistakes.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">LIVERPOOL</span>&nbsp; Are there complications with older Liverpool properties?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>Yes. Liverpool has one of the highest concentrations of Victorian and Edwardian housing in England. Many have gravity-fed systems, back boilers, chimneys used as flue routes and pipe runs that differ from modern builds. Our engineers are experienced with Liverpool's specific housing stock. We know what to expect before we open a wall. The free survey is essential for any older Liverpool property.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">TIME</span>&nbsp; How long does a boiler installation take?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>A straight like-for-like combi swap takes 4 to 6 hours. Done in a single day. Bigger jobs take 1 to 3 days. Same-day and next-day install for urgent swaps across Liverpool. We confirm timing at the free survey.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">WARRANTY</span>&nbsp; What warranty do I get with a new boiler?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>Every install carries a 12-month workmanship guarantee for peace of mind. The manufacturer warranty depends on the boiler model and installer accreditation. Standard manufacturer warranties typically run 2 to 5 years on most models. Longer warranties up to 10 years are offered by Worcester Bosch and Vaillant when fitted by an accredited installer and serviced yearly. We register the manufacturer warranty on your behalf on install day.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">FLUSH</span>&nbsp; Do I need a power flush before my new boiler?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>In most cases yes. Particularly if your system is more than 5 years old. All major makers need a clean system as a warranty condition. We do the power flush before connecting the new boiler to protect the heat exchanger from day one. A power flush costs from £350 and comes as a bundle with your new boiler at a better combined price.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">GRANTS</span>&nbsp; Is there a grant for a new boiler in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>Liverpool homeowners on qualifying benefits including Universal Credit and Pension Credit may qualify for the <a href="https://www.gov.uk/apply-great-british-insulation-scheme" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ECO4 scheme</a>. It can fund a full boiler replacement. The <a href="https://www.gov.uk/apply-boiler-upgrade-scheme" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Boiler Upgrade Scheme</a> gives grants of up to £7,500 towards a heat pump. We check your eligibility at the free survey at no cost.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">GAS SAFE</span>&nbsp; Are you Gas Safe registered?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>Yes. Liverpool Emergency Plumber is Gas Safe registered. Verify at <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gassaferegister.co.uk</a>. Every install is done by Gas Safe registered engineers. All gas work is carried out by Gas Safe registered engineers. A Gas Safe registered engineer is required by law for all home gas work in the UK.</p></div></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

